# The hero's standing shot, both directions, read off the fire path.
#
# The aim loop and the fire branch make these unambiguous. Left (CAVES):
#
#     LABEL_E87C:                      <- the aim loop
#         break
#         je [HERO_ACTION_POS_MASK], 0x80, LABEL_E8AA
#         call LABEL_99EB              <- HERO_STAND_AIM_LEFT + its charge dot
#         je [HERO_ACTION_POS_MASK], 0x00, LABEL_E87C
#     LABEL_E8AA:                      <- the fire button
#         call LABEL_9A15              <- CV_3A96, drawn AT the shot
#         mov [0x21], [HERO_X] / mov [0x27], [HERO_Y]
#         sub [0x21], 0x001E           <- the muzzle, to the LEFT
#         sub [0x27], 0x0027
#         call LABEL_6265              <- the projectile is spawned
#         break
#         call LABEL_99D9              <- CV_391A, the frame after
#
# and the right is the same routine mirrored, with `add [0x21], 0x001E`:
# CV_3858 at the shot, CV_36D2 after it.
#
# Two independent checks agree. mirror_match.py scores CV_3A96 against
# CV_3858 at 0.592 and CV_391A against CV_36D2 at 0.530, both inside the
# 0.520..0.923 band its control measures for pairs a person named from other
# evidence, while the cross pairings score 1.768 and 2.250. And the widths
# reproduce the crouch family exactly -- AIM 44 / F0 44 / F1 36 there,
# aim 40 / F0 40 / F1 34 here.
#
# The F1 frame doubles as the aim-exit frame: CAPSULE's LABEL_97D4 leaves the
# aim loop through it too. `SHOOT_..._F1` follows the crouch family's own
# vocabulary for the same role rather than inventing a second word.
#
# CV_5C54 is blinked by the right aim loop under the identical test the left
# one uses, and the dot offsets settle the direction: the crouch dots are
# 0x5C4C (right) and 0x5C94 (left), and the standing ones sit exactly 8 bytes
# after each.
#
# CV_15DC is drawn on the way out of the right aim loop, after CV_36D2 and
# immediately before `jmp HERO_WALK_RIGHT_LOOP` -- 14 wide against the aim's
# 40, the arm back down.
#
# Still held: CV_367C, a 7x18 three-leaf gun-arm layer of the same shape as
# every HERO_GUN_ARM_RIGHT_CASE_*, with nothing to say which pose it belongs
# to.
CV_3A96 HERO_STAND_SHOOT_LEFT_F0
CV_391A HERO_STAND_SHOOT_LEFT_F1
CV_3858 HERO_STAND_SHOOT_RIGHT_F0
CV_36D2 HERO_STAND_SHOOT_RIGHT_F1
CV_5C54 HERO_STAND_AIM_RIGHT_CHARGE_DOT
CV_15DC HERO_STAND_GUN_LOWER_RIGHT
